5. S1-mini  — transcript normalization model (GGUF, downloaded at runtime)
   https://huggingface.co/superwhisper/s1-mini
   License: Apache License 2.0, plus an additional naming term
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Zee's auto-correct pass runs "S1-mini" by "Superwhisper", a Qwen3-0.6B
fine-tune that rewrites raw ASR output as clean written text (fillers removed,
punctuation and capitalization applied, spoken numbers and dates written out).

  Source:  https://huggingface.co/superwhisper/s1-mini
  Base:    Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B — https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B
  License: Apache-2.0 — http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0
           plus the ADDITIONAL TERM reproduced below.

Changes made: the released weights were quantized to q4_k_m for use with
llama.cpp. The weights themselves were not otherwise modified.

ADDITIONAL TERM (reproduced verbatim from the model's LICENSE):

   In addition to the terms of the Apache License, Version 2.0 above: any
   use, distribution, or integration of this model, whether unmodified or
   as part of a derivative work or product, must continue to identify it
   by its original name, "S1-mini" by "Superwhisper", using that exact
   capitalization, regardless of any other name under which the model or
   a product incorporating it is marketed or distributed.

Accordingly, Zee identifies this component as "S1-mini" by "Superwhisper"
wherever it is named: the -autocorrect flag help, the diagnostics log, and
this file. The user-facing tray item is named for the feature ("Auto-correct"),
not for the model.
